1
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:23,700
 Stars, galaxies, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace.

2
00:00:24,020 --> 00:01:32,980
 Man over wings is such a wondrous thing.

3
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:40,100
 Behind the deuce of rumsy, come take your place.

4
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:41,700
 We're leaving soon.

5
00:01:50,730 --> 00:02:28,610
 Vibrations, maybe it's the power source.

6
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,920
 It's probably the power generator for the city.

7
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:31,800
 Could be in this area.

8
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,730
 Would have to be enormous, wouldn't it?

9
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:35,410
 I'm thinking of Murdoch.

10
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,430
 Poor fellow's probably dead out there.

11
00:02:37,690 --> 00:02:40,060
 You can think of him, but now's not the time.

12
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,210
 What happened exactly?

13
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,560
 What's your analysis of the situation, Metro?

14
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,840
 No analysis possible, not enough data.

15
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:51,080
 I believe that I do have sufficient grasp of the situation to suggest that we are not among friends.

16
00:02:51,560 --> 00:03:00,000
 Notice.

17
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:04,060
 Looks like those robots, well, looks like they're not programmed to detect us.

18
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:44,050
 Instantly, my friend.

19
00:03:56,320 --> 00:04:09,310
 Message received.

20
00:04:10,010 --> 00:04:12,770
 Encountering Omega ship in 20 minutes, great computer.

21
00:04:13,150 --> 00:04:14,300
 What are your orders?

22
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:18,190
 Activate preparations for receiving our guests.

23
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:27,580
 Question, Colonel, regarding our outer perimeter defense system.

24
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:29,920
 there was a local activation. What was that?

25
00:04:30,590 --> 00:04:32,390
 The power network was overloaded

26
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:34,070
 at takeoff. We suppose it resulted

27
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:36,610
 in certain short circuits. I see.

28
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:38,900
 This must be rectified in future.

29
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:40,860
 Yes, great computer.

30
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:52,220
 You're still worried? Yes, I am, maestro.

31
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:55,220
 Our children. What's happened to them?

32
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,920
 What about them? Yes, yes, of course,

33
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,140
 it's worrying, but with this ship, you'll be able

34
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:02,000
 to meet any eventuality we encounter.

35
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,580
 Colonel, a massive asteroid is directly

36
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,520
 in our flight path. It's rather curious, sir.

37
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,320
 It's coming straight for us and not spinning.

38
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:12,000
 Our computer maintains it's discovered

39
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,860
 a source of heat combustion. Colonel, it's a spaceship. A spaceship of that size? No.

40
00:05:18,910 --> 00:05:24,110
 So surely there's no such ship. Maximum power on the observation screen. Fire a sunlight rocket

41
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:41,480
 to light it up. Welcome you to our nebula, visitors from Omega. Men from Omega. Welcome

42
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:46,060
 you as friends. We request you follow our instructions very carefully and of prime

43
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:51,260
 importance. We give you our unequivocal promise that no harm will come to you, but we must

44
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:56,160
 insist on one condition. At the slightest hostile action on your part, we will be obliged to

45
00:05:56,160 --> 00:06:01,800
 destroy you. So far, so good. Got any idea where Psyche is? It would seem that we are going in the

46
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:06,400
 right direction generally, but this place is so strange I cannot be sure of anything. Well,

47
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:10,300
 you'd better figure it out soon. I can't take it much longer in this tin suit. In that case,

48
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:59,590
 I would suggest you. Specialists has devised a special treatment that will cure you. Please

49
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:06,820
 cooperate. Oh, Mr. Nuts and Bolts, the treatment is over. Exactly, it's over. Except for one little

50
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:35,510
 dose of your own medicine. And already? No, Pio. We're traveling out in space. In space, you say?

51
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:37,260
 A whole building in space?

52
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:40,760
 Not only a building, Piero. The entire city.

53
00:07:41,250 --> 00:07:48,000
 Yes, sorry about that. I knew what that rumbling was. It had to be a ship taking off, but I didn't think it was the right time to talk about it.

54
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:50,810
 Good old Metro. What would we do without you?

55
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:54,700
 Long way, but I found you. How do they treat you here?

56
00:07:56,080 --> 00:08:07,700
 Piero, I'm fine now that you're here. Now that you're both here. But you know, it's curious. For a little while now, I've had the feeling that there are friends nearby, and not just you two.

57
00:08:08,230 --> 00:08:10,210
 Here? In the city, you mean?

58
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:10,770
 Mm-hmm.

59
00:08:11,850 --> 00:08:16,110
 I don't wish to spoil the mood, but if they are here, shouldn't we set about finding them?

60
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:16,840
 Eh?

61
00:08:27,130 --> 00:09:16,460
 These are the senior officers of our spaceship.

62
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:23,730
 Maestro is our leading scientist, and I am Colonel Pierre, chief of the Omega Intergalactic Police.

63
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:25,220
 Why can't we see you?

64
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:27,200
 Because I am a computer.

65
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:29,710
 I am the great computer.

66
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:32,130
 I am present in all parts of this city.

67
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:33,110
 I am this city.

68
00:09:33,530 --> 00:09:35,760
 I am all that you have seen here and more.

69
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:44,450
 But to give you real beings to talk with, I have produced others like you.

70
00:09:44,530 --> 00:09:47,970
 You will feel more comfortable addressing individuals whom you can see.

71
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:49,820
 I shall speak through them.

72
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:52,670
 Well now, Colonel, go on.

73
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:53,930
 Ask your questions.

74
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,520
 I shall answer anything you care to ask.

75
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,600
 And of course, your questions too, sir.

76
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,660
 How is it possible?

77
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,290
 How can there be a computer city?

78
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:06,560
 I am electronically linked to all things in all places at all times.

79
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,160
 Each of my creations is linked to me.

80
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,240
 Even to your soldiers?

81
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:10,320
 To your robots?

82
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:14,050
 No, not to the relatively unimportant ones, workers' tools, such things.

83
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:18,430
 I would like to know who built you, created you, who programmed you.

84
00:10:18,710 --> 00:10:22,430
 That is a long story, but surely one that you will have to hear, so I shall tell you.

85
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:28,070
 One day, over three centuries ago, there was a very important meeting on Earth.

86
00:10:29,090 --> 00:10:32,870
 And so, once more, our planet is at the brink of chaos, the prey of the ambitious,

87
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:35,230
 the intolerant dictators hungry for conquest.

88
00:10:35,490 --> 00:10:39,370
 Our world's survival can be achieved only by the machine, by my machine.

89
00:10:39,590 --> 00:10:41,270
 Allow my computer to rule the world.

90
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:43,770
 Allow it to determine all laws in our society.

91
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:48,330
 And without envy or bias, it will peacefully carry out a just and lasting policy

92
00:10:48,330 --> 00:10:49,970
 to regulate the affairs of all men.

93
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:50,970
 Peace forever.

94
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:52,960
 Yeah, peace forever.

95
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,020
 Peace of the grave.

96
00:10:54,450 --> 00:10:56,260
 Why, machines governing the world?

97
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:57,380
 That's immoral.

98
00:10:57,810 --> 00:11:00,670
 And would you rather have the morality of human jackals?

99
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:03,490
 There is give and take in human feelings and understanding.

100
00:11:03,670 --> 00:11:06,490
 Would you have all human beings classified by machines?

101
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:10,000
 And metaphysics, that superior faculty of man,

102
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,080
 have you considered that?

103
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:12,270
 Stuff and nonsense.

104
00:11:12,430 --> 00:11:13,250
 You are all idiots.

105
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:16,750
 You are the idiot who can't really stand.

106
00:11:17,690 --> 00:11:18,510
 Crazy.

107
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:20,040
 Crazy.

108
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,020
 They must be crazy to think I'm crazy.

109
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:25,670
 This is an interesting nebula here.

110
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:29,760
 And it holds endless quantities of metal, I judge.

111
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:38,870
 Go and gather some samples of metals.

112
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:40,510
 All you have to do is pick them up.

113
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:51,770
 Soon we will start constructing a new generator.

114
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:53,180
 And relax then.

115
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:51,290
 To visit the neighbor's vicious animals and worst of all, little food.

116
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:52,980
 I can certainly help you.

117
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,980
 If you like, you can come to my planet.

118
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:55,660
 To Yama.

119
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,900
 Living conditions are much better there.

120
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:01,800
 You can establish your own base, which will provide you with all your needs.

121
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:03,330
 Healthy robot!

122
00:13:11,590 --> 00:13:18,590
 What is it you want, my friends?

123
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:24,040
 Now, you listen, Professor. We think it's wrong what you're doing just making all these good-for-nothing robots

124
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,850
 when you ought to use your brains to do what you can for us.

125
00:13:26,850 --> 00:13:32,060
 But I do nothing else. You may not understand, but I assure you, everything I do is for you.

126
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:36,240
 I welcome you aboard. Haven't I said that I will do all I can for you, my friends?

127
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:39,360
 You're no friend of ours. Your only friends are machines.

128
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:42,770
 Now, once and for all, will you put your knowledge to our use?

129
00:13:42,770 --> 00:13:45,660
 So it all starts again, just as it did back on Earth.

130
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,350
 No, I will not aid your ambition.

131
00:13:47,350 --> 00:13:49,920
 Watch this!

132
00:13:49,920 --> 00:14:37,660
 Attachment of soldiers to construct a base to keep watch over the men there,

133
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:39,690
 otherwise it will start all over again.

134
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:42,870
 You can speak, you will explain it to them.

135
00:14:42,870 --> 00:14:44,960
 And should they not agree?

136
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,960
 So much the worse for them, you will be armed.

137
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:48,960
 What happens to those few matters?

138
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:51,970
 As you order.

139
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:54,970
 And for a long time thereafter, our city, shielded from men's mad designs,

140
00:14:54,970 --> 00:14:56,970
 grew in strength inside the walls.

141
00:14:56,970 --> 00:14:58,940
 Control center at its heart.

142
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:47,170
 Concepts that can only elude me.

143
00:15:47,170 --> 00:15:49,700
 Expeed attention, your implacable logic.

144
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:55,290
 Men are weak, so weak fight with them to make them accept what is good for them.

145
00:15:55,810 --> 00:16:00,250
 It is for that only that I have ever used force, and you are to use force only in that end.

146
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:01,440
 The welfare of mankind.

147
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:03,130
 Remember, it's your only objective.

148
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:05,790
 You seek to give eternal peace to man.

149
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:09,310
 Thy will shall be done.

150
00:16:11,230 --> 00:16:19,380
 He died some two centuries ago, since all of us here have remained faithful to his original programming.

151
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:24,850
 Look around you, our entire city has been constructed in his image, for we honor the memory of our crew.

152
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:31,140
 Our city grew in size, developed great resources, all with the objective he set.

153
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:34,850
 And now all our testing has been approaching our goal.

154
00:16:35,390 --> 00:16:36,790
 You're testing? What tests?

155
00:16:36,930 --> 00:16:38,190
 You are acquainted with some.

156
00:16:38,390 --> 00:16:40,990
 In the attempt to take over the Cosmopolitan, was that you?

157
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:41,650
 Yes.

158
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:45,270
 Hold to the robots on the planet Leto as well.

159
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,710
 Yes, with the complicity of the Cassiopeians.

160
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,560
 We had to practice being around you.

161
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:54,110
 Those were only exercises, maneuvers to perfect our technique.

162
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:56,660
 Cassiopeia's an ally of yours.

163
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,100
 An ally when it suited us.

164
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,000
 They think they are manipulating us, but they do our bidding.

165
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:03,230
 You don't know General Grouchley, I'm afraid.

166
00:17:03,350 --> 00:17:04,850
 You do not know me, Colonel.

167
00:17:05,410 --> 00:17:10,170
 General is a driven, frustrated creature dominated by his insane desire to rule the universe.

168
00:17:10,290 --> 00:17:13,440
 He is exactly the sort of man against whom I must defend humanity.

169
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:17,380
 And you, you'd carry it out at all costs?

170
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:18,960
 I will carry out my duty at all costs.

171
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,500
 The rocket bomb against the Earth, was that you?

172
00:17:21,690 --> 00:17:23,500
 It was us with help from Cassiopeia.

173
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:26,520
 And so, you would have destroyed the Earth.

174
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:29,180
 It was the General's intention, not ours.

175
00:17:30,930 --> 00:17:32,410
 Contrary to our own interests.

176
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:36,220
 No, we wanted only to measure your capacity to resist our attack.

177
00:17:36,350 --> 00:17:39,190
 Had you surrendered, valuable time would have been saved.

178
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:43,170
 In any case, our bomb was not programmed to explode. It would have caused no harm.

179
00:17:43,930 --> 00:17:49,900
 I would like to know our reconnaissance vehicle, Hummingbird, that happened to come into your nebula.

180
00:17:50,350 --> 00:17:51,330
 What happened to it?

181
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:55,380
 It crashed accidentally on planet Apis. It is our sister planet.

182
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:58,310
 What? And what about its crew?

183
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:01,890
 Wounded, we located the young lady and have tried to cure her.

184
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:06,400
 Our best doctors are caring for her. One minute, I will get a report on her condition.

185
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:08,070
 What about the young man?

186
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:14,820
 Captain Piero, unfortunately, was lost attempting to cross the dangerous swamps of planet Aptis.

187
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:18,890
 The part of my death is premature, great computer.

188
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:25,140
 Piero.

189
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,340
 Oh, well, I'm used to this.

190
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:30,400
 In all these emotional scenes, everybody's hugged except you know who.

191
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:35,840
 I assure you I am pleased to know that you have recovered one who was lost, Colonel.

192
00:18:36,670 --> 00:18:39,160
 No thanks to the treatment you subjected me to.

193
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:39,920
 My regrets.

194
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,020
 For us, all that counts is the final result.

195
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:46,830
 The tranquility of the universe, the lot of certain individuals, is of no interest.

196
00:18:46,890 --> 00:18:52,770
 us and a lot of some thousands of individuals judging from the way the yaman people are allowed

197
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:58,750
 to live the condition of even thousands cannot matter well then what do you want may i suggest

198
00:18:58,750 --> 00:19:04,130
 that before continuing our discussion we make a brief tour of the city i believe you will understand

199
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:51,620
 better fantastic masters spaceship enshrined in a crystal as a mausoleum in a word incredible it's

200
00:19:51,620 --> 00:20:03,580
 the only word may find it even more unbelievable this block is composed of 40 stories here too

201
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:12,900
 what I am. Billion upon billion, integrated circuit, data storage files, controlling a universe

202
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:24,290
 posed to billions of individuals. This is beyond belief. There it is. There is perhaps no need to

203
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:30,690
 show you our factories, our weapons. You have already gathered enough data to judge our power.

204
00:20:31,410 --> 00:20:37,150
 These weapons, who taught you how to make them? Your master, of course. No, we possessed only

205
00:20:37,150 --> 00:20:43,060
 rudimentary weapons. But when General Grouchley asked us to manufacture them, I realized how

206
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:48,680
 possession of these arms could accelerate the process of achieving our goal. And did he share

207
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:53,710
 all of his secrets with you? Not intentionally. The general takes himself for a very clever fellow.

208
00:20:53,830 --> 00:20:58,720
 He tried to keep secret certain critical data. We were able to extrapolate and interpolate and in

209
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:03,050
 the end we were able not only to perfect his weapons but to improve them, amplify them. Today

210
00:21:03,050 --> 00:21:09,000
 we manufacture weapons as powerful as we wish. Power to infinity. Once again my question is what

211
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:13,970
 do you want of us? Despite his extraordinary capacity for knowledge man is in his infancy.

212
00:21:13,970 --> 00:21:15,590
 he refuses to grow to maturity.

213
00:21:16,330 --> 00:21:20,170
 War is still for him a game in which he can give full reign to his baser instincts.

214
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:21,560
 This we cannot allow.

215
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:25,460
 We will not allow mankind to be subjected to suffering or privation.

216
00:21:26,090 --> 00:21:28,610
 Under our governance, all source of conflict will be eliminated.

217
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,490
 If Grouchly weren't around, there wouldn't be conflict.

218
00:21:31,690 --> 00:21:33,090
 There is a Grouchly in every man.

219
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:36,880
 What I've seen of your governance is less convincing than your words.

220
00:21:37,290 --> 00:21:40,070
 And what I was made to suffer doesn't reassure me either.

221
00:21:40,470 --> 00:21:41,570
 You are confused.

222
00:21:41,870 --> 00:21:44,750
 To achieve our objective, we must be effective.

223
00:21:44,750 --> 00:21:52,170
 and more cruel than the cruelty you claim to be fighting millions of years ago you humanity came

224
00:21:52,170 --> 00:21:56,970
 out of your caves and what has happened your instincts what real human progress have you made

225
00:21:56,970 --> 00:22:02,970
 here you may judge for yourself what we have accomplished in less than three centuries one

226
00:22:02,970 --> 00:22:07,570
 moment one moment you were created programmed by a man you are not going to tell me that a creation

227
00:22:07,570 --> 00:22:13,000
 can be greater than what created it right our creator was an exceptional man hence we are

228
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:21,290
 exception. As for man, it requires only a planet, an ocean, a sun, and there are 200 billion in our

229
00:22:21,290 --> 00:22:27,150
 galaxy alone. All this and in time man emerges as the final link in the chain, and for all of this

230
00:22:27,150 --> 00:22:35,590
 he may still consider himself unique. Precisely, man is unique. He alone in creation can abstract

231
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:40,120
 from his experience. He alone believes in what he cannot see. All your abstract beliefs are to give

232
00:22:40,120 --> 00:22:44,860
 a meaning to your existence. Only man can laugh, sing, do what he will for fun, not out of necessity.

233
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:49,220
 Whoever saw a robot compose a Mozart sonata or a Beethoven quartet?

234
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:50,560
 It could be done.

235
00:22:51,070 --> 00:22:51,950
 But what would be the point?

236
00:22:52,330 --> 00:22:55,750
 All music is no more than man's effort to lose himself in infinity.

237
00:22:55,910 --> 00:22:57,610
 It is a delusion, a dream, an escape.

238
00:22:58,140 --> 00:23:01,060
 I do believe I have heard that someplace before.

239
00:23:01,670 --> 00:23:04,130
 I repeat, you must submit to our government.

240
00:23:04,330 --> 00:23:05,810
 In any case, you have no choice.

241
00:23:06,450 --> 00:23:12,070
 According to my calculations, chances are 99.99 in our favor in the event of conflict.

242
00:23:12,070 --> 00:23:15,950
 Allow me to show you what you would face.

243
00:24:06,990 --> 00:24:07,490
 Any planet.

244
00:24:09,950 --> 00:24:13,150
 No, that's not necessary. I can certify to its power. I've seen it in action.

245
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:37,280
 All sorts of weapons. Our protection shield field of force is totally invulnerable, as you will have observed.

246
00:24:39,070 --> 00:24:40,410
 If you say so.

247
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:47,180
 Really have to extend your power over a few more rocks in the sky, the Confederation of Omega?

248
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:50,580
 Haven't you enough? All those billions of other systems in the galaxy?

249
00:24:50,580 --> 00:24:57,450
 We have no choice. Otherwise, the germ of man's aggression will still live, and one day man will again threaten the...

250
00:24:57,450 --> 00:24:59,450
 You are worse than those you would blame.

251
00:24:59,710 --> 00:25:03,490
 But we have neither ambition, nor passion, nor madness.

252
00:25:03,690 --> 00:25:06,780
 Why not accept? You know quite well that you will not be allowed to choose.

253
00:25:07,150 --> 00:25:08,710
 Don't make us inflict any harm.

254
00:25:09,050 --> 00:25:12,950
 We here are not authorized to engage the Confederation in any such decision.

255
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:15,540
 In my opinion, they'll never accept.

256
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:19,440
 Yes. In all honesty, their acceptance is highly unlikely.

257
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:24,110
 But it's only logical. You do realize that you would have no chance against us.

258
00:25:24,830 --> 00:25:28,890
 Yes, I'll admit that. However, in no way does that change what I have just said.

259
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:34,430
 Very well. Return home. Carry my message with you. Tell them what you have seen.

260
00:25:35,090 --> 00:25:38,440
 We will come soon to know your answer. We will arrive in force.

261
00:25:38,950 --> 00:25:44,220
 First, we have a matter to settle. I understand that Cassiopeia is no longer a member of your confederation.

262
00:25:45,170 --> 00:25:46,540
 But go now, free.

